{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479701-other-werewolf-option","id":1479701,"title":"Other werewolf option","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-29T09:01:11-07:00","id":1479701,"title":"Other werewolf option","content":"One of the most curious things I realised WtA is missing, is an alternative to the garou.<br /> <br /> Not the Changing Breeds. but another type of werewolf. Vampire, Mage and Changeling run the gamut of different types of vampires, mages and fae. But werewolf instead is stuck with only the garou as werewolves.<br /> <br /> And, personally, I think that is a loss on WtA's part. I am a big fan of the NWoD way of not tying everything into one mythology and I feel having a more 'traditional' werewolf would do good as a contrast to the garou. On top of everything, it would stop the recent push to make the garou fit a peg they were never meant to fit.<br /> <br /> So what do I mean by 'traditional' werewolf?<br /> <br /> The person starts as a human and is then turned into a werewolf through infection, curse or wearing a wolf-skin.<br /> <br /> The ability to change forms is tied to the method they became werewolves. I.e. Those wearing wolf-skin can shift whenever, the infected are bound to change without control,etc.<br /> <br /> The forms are limited to one or two.<br /> <br /> The morality of the werewolves is not tied to Gaia/Wyrm but instead various per person.<br /> <br /> They cannot access the umbra or gain gifts from the spirits, instead, the powers would be mastering their nature better.<br /> <br /> This is very rough, but I do feel it'd give people not into the Ecoterrorist Furry Captain Planet something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T09:58:51-07:00","id":1479711,"title":"","content":"There are numerous other ways that werewolves could be done in an RPG that are different from Garou in W:tA. The issue is, I think, is that if you're playing some other sort of shape shifter who isn't a Garou, then that character isn't really going to have any place in a W:tA chronicle and the splat isn't going to have much overlap with Garou even if they have some similar abilities. So I think it would be interesting to have different kinds of werewolves as NPC's in a Mage or Vampire game, for example, but in a standard W:tA game they might be out of place.<br /> <br /> If I were doing a very different sort of werewolf, I think I would have them essentially be mystics of sorts, maybe even shamans with a tie in to some of the spirit stuff in W:tA, but not a separate race. A shaman with a spiritual connection to wolves who learns a spell that allows for transformation into a wolf. If we go with one of the myths, the ritual to transform could involve a wolf skin or this could be done with other animals as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T10:35:45-07:00","id":1479716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479701-other-werewolf-option?p=1479711#post1479711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are numerous other ways that werewolves could be done in an RPG that are different from Garou in W:tA. The issue is, I think, is that if you're playing some other sort of shape shifter who isn't a Garou, then that character isn't really going to have any place in a W:tA chronicle and the splat isn't going to have much overlap with Garou even if they have some similar abilities. So I think it would be interesting to have different kinds of werewolves as NPC's in a Mage or Vampire game, for example, but in a standard W:tA game they might be out of place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think this could be changed. So much of WtA is tied into the Gaia vs Wyrm war and there is little alternative to that type of game. But there are many people who aren't really into the 'captain planet' stuff and just want to play werewolves without that. This is why I feel more focus on both ronin and maybe a more typical werewolf splat would serve better.<br /> <br /> Because things like lessening the umbra, the Bite and such, they do not fit the garou well. But if there was something else to serve as the Bitten Werewolf fantasy, the garou could stay garou.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T14:54:03-07:00","id":1479748,"title":"","content":"I think you're overstating the case of the rest of the WoD a bit here.<br /> <br /> Core book VtM vampires don't deal with &quot;other kinds of vampires.&quot; Until Kindred of the East was published it was assumed all vampires worked on the same principles even with local variations (remember there were two retconned Japanese Clans before KotE). There being other &quot;vampires&quot; out in the WoD is something that comes from supplements, other game-lines, and so on. <br /> <br /> The nWoD/CofD isn't any different here. The Uratha of Forsaken don't have Skinchangers as a default antagonist... those show up in a general supplement about how to model the &quot;wear an animal skin to change into that animal&quot; types.<br /> <br /> The problem here isn't WtA, it's that the cWoD never did all of the &quot;monster building books for mortal/minor supernaturals to face off against,&quot; that the nWoD/CofD has. And at this point.. why change the cWoD? It's a nostalgia brand for people that want to play the games it popularized in the 90s. There are lots of a horror RPGs, and plenty of them that let you play the monsters, and lots of them do their own spin on how their versions of those monsters work (including the CofD). There's competition now that just didn't exist in the past, and &quot;we rough fit this other idea into our already popular game,&quot; isn't a selling point for anything that's not D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> How many people is this really for at this point? If it was thirty years ago, your points would have a lot more weight. Now, it's a lot smaller potential population of people that are going to care. You have the old school WoD fans that for some reason want this but haven't already made it happen using the scattered tools for doing so (Just giving core book powers of other splats to mortals via a metaphysical process, the various supernatural object building systems, Numina, the various splat-oriented monster building systems for custom non-core supernatural critters) and refuse to move onto different systems that have this more built in, and... potentially some portion of new players that would gladly pick the cWoD over all the other options if only it had better defined &quot;other&quot; werewolves?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T16:14:32-07:00","id":1479757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479701-other-werewolf-option#post1479701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is very rough, but I do feel it'd give people not into the Ecoterrorist Furry Captain Planet something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That description, perhaps with the exception of the furry part. has typically fit Mage better than Werewolf, what with no one in Captain Planet ever tearing Hoggish Greedly or Looten Plunder in half like a wet paper towel full of blood (fun fact, when Garou shout &quot;heart&quot;, they typically refer to what they're going to remove!), or how the Gaia of Captain Planet acts like a shared avatar for five mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T00:03:12-07:00","id":1479789,"title":"","content":"I've done a lot of work in my chronicles to introduce the feel of more traditional werewolves among Garou. I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/314196-werewolf-and-original-sources-folklore\">a thread about traditional werewolves and original folklore</a> as one of my first posts on this forum. I also supplemented it with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1445567-lycanthropic-flowers\">later threads such as this</a>. My work aren't the only methods available, but I found it to have worked well for me.<br /> <br /> Want to include wolf straps and such in your chronicle? Make it a Fetish that improves transformation speed and acts like the rite of talisman dedication.<br /> <br /> Want to include wolf salves and other ointments that witches used to transform into wolves? Treat it like a Talen or the end product of the Rite of Spirit Brew.<br /> <br /> Want werewolves biting people to allow transformation? Say that it's a way that Garou have found useful to activate the First Change for a lot of Lost Cubs or Lunatics who are having trouble changing.<br /> <br /> Want the drinking of lycanthropic streams or eating of lycanthropic flowers to activate? Say those are examples of Wyld Fetishes that help provoke the First Change in the same way.<br /> <br /> Some of these methods might result in Ronin who are technically Garou, but some of them form societies with very different ideas about their condition than what the Garou Nation has, and these can emulate some traditional stories of werewolves. Instead of talking about &quot;Kinfolk&quot; they talk about &quot;cursed bloodlines&quot; where the curse is passed down through the blood, able to erupt at any time.<br /> <br /> I also make Lunatics more common.<br /> <br /> I also make in my chronicles that Skin Changers are far older and far more common than canon. Sam Haight was not the inventor of the method. At best he was a rediscoverer of a secret the Garou try to repress. But there are plenty of very old wolfskins handed down from generation to generation of lost kinfolk who act as counterparts to the official Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> Then there are Fomori and Kami that transform ordinary humans into monsters who can shapechange into wolves. If it is a Fomori, then obviously it's an antagonist that they'll kill. But a Kami would be an ally.<br /> <br /> And small groups like the Fenians of the original WoD: Sorcerer who know the Path of Shapechanging, but are limited to being wolves and often requiring focuses like actual wolf pelts. They're not Garou, but they're what ordinary people would still consider to be werewolves. Garou hold them in disdain, but also see them as useful allies at the same time.<br /> <br /> I'm also big on using the existing Merits and Flaws that mirror traditional and cinematic werewolves. I openly encourage players to use them for their PCs, and I often give them out to NPCs especially those of Pure Breed. If players see them as relatively common (I try for a 25-33% ration of NPCs having at least one of them), they begin to see those Merits/Flaws as normal.<br /> <br /> This keeps things in the chronicle heavily based on existing Werewolf: the Apocalypse concepts, but creates the feel of more traditional werewolves. It's mainly a matter of some creativity and how the ST presents information to the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T00:14:51-07:00","id":1479793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479701-other-werewolf-option?p=1479748#post1479748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How many people is this really for at this point? If it was thirty years ago, your points would have a lot more weight. Now, it's a lot smaller potential population of people that are going to care. You have the old school WoD fans that for some reason want this but haven't already made it happen using the scattered tools for doing so (Just giving core book powers of other splats to mortals via a metaphysical process, the various supernatural object building systems, Numina, the various splat-oriented monster building systems for custom non-core supernatural critters) and refuse to move onto different systems that have this more built in, and... potentially some portion of new players that would gladly pick the cWoD over all the other options if only it had better defined &quot;other&quot; werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more a thought exercise than anything else. But to answer your question: Clearly there is want if BNS introduced the Bite. While that was done to allow adult PCs to change into garou, it still shows a type of story missing from WtA.<br /> <br /> I did not make this thread to actually work on an alternative to the garou. More just a look into how WtA never quite gave players the option to play out a less gaia/wyrm story.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479701-other-werewolf-option?p=1479757#post1479757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That description, perhaps with the exception of the furry part. has typically fit Mage better than Werewolf, what with no one in Captain Planet ever tearing Hoggish Greedly or Looten Plunder in half like a wet paper towel full of blood (fun fact, when Garou shout &quot;heart&quot;, they typically refer to what they're going to remove!), or how the Gaia of Captain Planet acts like a shared avatar for five mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, I agree. That is just the phrase often used to deride WtA. I don't agree with it a bit, because it implies that caring for the environment is cringe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T17:26:37-07:00","id":1479848,"title":"","content":"As Black Fox said the intentional changes ( hide/belt/ritual etc.) are pretty handily covered by Sorcerers. The accidental blackout monster that leaves you waking up with a mouthful of sheeps wool and no memory once a month could be anything from Spirit Possession/Curse/Fomori.<br /> <br /> The Sorcerer version can be a fun game, essentially playing in a Kinfolk/Hunter Hunted level campaign. <br /> <br /> The latter is really just playing an Average Joe and handing your character sheet to the ST every 28 days of in-game, which might be an interesting one-shot but I can't see it holding interest for too long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T18:34:32-07:00","id":1479851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479701-other-werewolf-option#post1479701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the most curious things I realised WtA is missing, is an alternative to the garou.<br /> <br /> Not the Changing Breeds. but another type of werewolf. Vampire, Mage and Changeling run the gamut of different types of vampires, mages and fae. But werewolf instead is stuck with only the garou as werewolves.<br /> <br /> And, personally, I think that is a loss on WtA's part. I am a big fan of the NWoD way of not tying everything into one mythology and I feel having a more 'traditional' werewolf would do good as a contrast to the garou. On top of everything, it would stop the recent push to make the garou fit a peg they were never meant to fit.<br /> <br /> So what do I mean by 'traditional' werewolf?<br /> <br /> The person starts as a human and is then turned into a werewolf through infection, curse or wearing a wolf-skin.<br /> <br /> The ability to change forms is tied to the method they became werewolves. I.e. Those wearing wolf-skin can shift whenever, the infected are bound to change without control,etc.<br /> <br /> The forms are limited to one or two.<br /> <br /> The morality of the werewolves is not tied to Gaia/Wyrm but instead various per person.<br /> <br /> They cannot access the umbra or gain gifts from the spirits, instead, the powers would be mastering their nature better.<br /> <br /> This is very rough, but I do feel it'd give people not into the Ecoterrorist Furry Captain Planet something.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that\u2019s a Hollywood werewolf, not a traditional one. But I have incorporated the idea at my own table with those Garou who completely reject their nature, and thus have no control over their shifting (2e Forsaken has this built into the system via being Harmony 10, completely divorced from your spirit-side). The infection angle (again, total Hollywood invention) is more complicated to incorporate, but I have some ideas for making the Garou as a whole not bloodline based.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T18:37:42-07:00","id":1479852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479701-other-werewolf-option?p=1479793#post1479793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yes, I agree. That is just the phrase often used to deride WtA. I don't agree with it a bit, because it implies that caring for the environment is cringe.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, when anthropogenic climate change is the greatest existential threat to human civilization as we know it, if not the survival of the species, it\u2019s pretty ridiculous to treat it as a childish topic.<br /> <br /> Biggest flaw of Captain Planet was that it had an unapologetically Malthusian episode, which is just factually wrong. I have no problem with Malthusian villains in Werewolf though so I keep that aspect of Garou society as something to keep in check. But I would like to give the Ratkin a rewrite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-30-2022, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T20:50:13-07:00","id":1479859,"title":"","content":"I'm one who's tired of the usual Gaia vs Wyrm theme of the Garou, although it has nothing to do with thinking it is a childish theme, but because I find the constant pressure of the war on the Wyrm overwhelming and limiting.<br /> <br /> But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, this is what this game is for, and there are other games out there to cover other approaches. De-emphasizing the war a bit could improve the Garou, maybe, and other things that can be Werewolves in their own way already exist, like those <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> mentioned, but beyond that what would even be the point?<br /> <br /> To just use the cWoD system for something else entirely, I prefer to just use something else, as this system isn't that great to begin with. I do have already the werewolves I want, it's called Forsaken. When I'm running or playing cWoD it is for its classic splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T08:16:27-07:00","id":1479895,"title":"","content":"Honestly if I wanted to play a different kind of werewolf I'd just use CoFD, Forsaken even has a couple of Wolf Blooded who hew closer to mythological or hollywood werewolves (although nobody gets the full on wolf-man).<br /> <br /> Yes the Gaia-Wyrm war can get tiresome, but to.me it's the point of playing Apocalypse over another game. The line both suffers and benefits from the focus, and while more support for Ronin games I'm not sure I'd ever use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 05-01-2022, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T13:14:40-07:00","id":1479906,"title":"","content":"Getting access to Dalu as part of a Wolf-Blooded Tell isn't full on Lon Chaney Jr., but it's pretty close and you get to put down, &quot;Badass Motherfucker,&quot; on your sheet.<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> And to the WtA things... even a Ronin game is caught up in the Gaia-Wyrm conflict. Ronin are targets of recruitment by the BSDs, and will get chased off (or worse) by Gaians if they don't act as mercenaries for Gaia's army. Being a Ronin that is free from the war is also a character with nothing to really do besides keep their Rage from messing up their life. It's sitting around playing a character that's actively trying to not do anything interesting... which is not really a great premise for a RPG.<br /> <br /> You could copy the Ghost Wolves of Forsaken rather than Ronin... but then why not just play Forsaken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T05:25:44-07:00","id":1479942,"title":"","content":"I stand corrected, you guys gave out good points about why this wouldn't work. As a note, I like WtA as it is, as I like Forsaken for what -it- is.<br /> <br /> My main reason for this thread was to think about how to bridge the gap between WtA as it is and the way BNS and W5 are going. Forsaken should be the default answer, of course.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T08:53:04-07:00","id":1479950,"title":"","content":"On the War vs the Wyrm getting tiresome front: There are still enemies besides the Wyrm. The Weaver is a major problem, not in any small part do to being responsible for the Wyrm becoming an issue in the first place. On the other hand, Spirits of the Wyld can also easily become major chronicle villains to throw a curve ball at the players.<br /> <br /> If you want to fight something other than &quot;evil side of Nature/Society&quot; there's Spectres serving Oblivion/The Grand Maw, Demons and Earthbound from DTF, Rogue mages, and Alien Fae. There's a wide net of demonic beings all fighting to be top dog of the Apocalyptic Dystopia they're all trying to turn the world into(and it's funny to think that one of reasons none have succeeded is because they all get in each other's way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T09:15:07-07:00","id":1479954,"title":"","content":"I think that both having a different kind of werewolf (like a curse spread through a bite) or a different setting focus (other than protecting the environment from the Wyrm) are reasonable goals. You could change W:tA so that being a Garou isn't hereditary but more mystical in origin, or maybe even spread through bites, though if it was spread through a bite then why wouldn't the Garou transform millions of people to better fight the Wyrm?<br /> <br /> You could heavily change the setting as well.<br /> <br /> One thing to keep in mind is that all WW games have cultures of supernatural creatures and motivations which tie into those cultures. Vampires have the struggles between the young and old, between rival Clans, the Camarilla fights the Sabbat, and so on. In Mage there is the battle over reality, mainly focused on the Technocracy vs the Tradition. In Werewolf, we have the battle against the Wyrm and its servants and allies.<br /> <br /> Removing the Captain Planet elements from your werewolf game is certainly possible, it's just that something else should be there to replace it. You could potentially keep a similar setting and make the Garou's primary enemy the Weaver - which actually makes sense in a lot of ways, though it may make the attitudes of the Garou seem even more extreme to the average human. You could actually remove all of that spiritual aspect from the game, it's just that a different sort of struggle should replace it, in which case you'd have an entirely different game. A similar concern exists for making the bite of a werewolf infectious, because then you would have a radically different culture that exists among the werewolves than one that currently exists in the Garou Nation. That isn't necessarily a bad thing, but it may require some thought and fleshing out. If anybody who survives a werewolf bite turns into a werewolf, then rather than being a dying race, Garou might have to strive to control their population.<br /> <br /> None of these things are bad or wrong, it's just that it would be creating a new game almost from the ground up, that are only similar in that their powers are similar.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T10:01:36-07:00","id":1479959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479701-other-werewolf-option?p=1479950#post1479950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the War vs the Wyrm getting tiresome front: There are still enemies besides the Wyrm</div> </div> </div> </div>There are, but what gets tiresome isn't the enemy, is the state of constant war itself and overwhelming presence of military concerns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T13:44:12-07:00","id":1479974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479701-other-werewolf-option?p=1479959#post1479959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are, but what gets tiresome isn't the enemy, is the state of constant war itself and overwhelming presence of military concerns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Garou defaulting to &quot;At War&quot; is unfortunately central to their purpose. Without an enemy to fight, they wouldn't really have anything to do.<br /> <br /> There are still other changing breeds though and the WtA setting is a place Designed for spiritual journeys about finding one's purpose and restoring lost pieces of history. For example:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Playing a troop of Gurahl on a quest to heal one of the fera breeds lost during the war of rage.</li> <li>An Ananasi trying to restore a weaver incarnae back to it former glory after being infected with it's masters madness, the entire journey being spent with a totem spirit of that incarnae's avatar attempting to aid them as it's main body's madness interferes, sabotaging some of their efforts with mis-directions, conflicting information, and wild goose-chases.</li> <li>A nuwasha desperately holding together a children's hospital as they juggle building a real relationship with the kids through their personal brand of comedy and trying to find solutions for the ever-growth abyss of debt they were saddled with when the previous director embezzled to funding and ran for Peru.</li> </ol>There are a number of ways you can tell a changing breed story that don't involve the Apocalypse. Particularly because it was never the other breed's jobs to participate in the first place, they only do so Now because of how Massively the Garou screwed things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T14:16:02-07:00","id":1479978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479701-other-werewolf-option?p=1479974#post1479974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a number of ways you can tell a changing breed story that don't involve the Apocalypse. Particularly because it was never the other breed's jobs to participate in the first place, they only do so Now because of how Massively the Garou screwed things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it matters for this specific thread, this runs into the problem of you not usually playing such stories with werewolves, they're not an option, and if they are they go back to have that pressure even if as background. You don't strictly have to play a war-oriented chronicle, but the war remains the focus of their society for whatever it's worth.<br /> <br /> But then again, I'm not trying to find a solution to this conundrum. I don't think that forcing new themes into W:tA should be done at all. I can play Forsaken when I want to play a more varied werewolf game, when I play WoD I want the Garou to be Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T16:24:46-07:00","id":1479988,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm going to have to agree that Forsaken is a much better generic werewolf game. But I don't think a stronger premise hurts Apocalypse, I get much more excited at the idea of running the game despite it having significant issues because of that focus.<br /> <br /> Out of the entirety of WoD and CofD the easiest game to come up with chronicle ideas for, for me at least, is Apocalypse (and the hardest are the Mage lines). If Apocalypse gets boring I can play Forsaken, or Requiem, or Lost, or any of the games in my collection (and that's quite a few games). If I want to do something radically different with werewolves, enough that Forsaken can't cover it, it might actually be better to just grab CofD or whatever system is suitable and build the werewolves from first principles (although I must admit, I really like the Forsaken forms).<br /> <br /> One of the games I'm planning does use quite different werewolves. But it doesn't use Apocalypse, I'll run it on CofD with PC werewolves being Wolf-blooded (if anybody wants to be one) and other werewolves just being built with whatever's needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}